@bio:

Joshua Albrecht is an Assistant Professor of Music Theory
at the University of Iowa in the United States. His
research focuses on digital and computational musicology,
along with perceptual and cognitive musicology. He has
published in the journals Music Perception, Empirical
Musicology Review, Journal of New Music Research, and Music
Theory Online, and has published chapters in the Oxford
Handbook of Music and Corpus Studies, and Historische
Musikwissenschaft in the Laaber-Verlag's Compendium Musik
series. He co-edits Empirical Musicology Review, and is
currently serving on the Executive Board of the Society for
Music Perception and Cognition. He also founded and runs
the Iowa Cognitive and Computational Musicology Lab at the
University of Iowa.


@@END: BIO